<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry II, Count of Rodez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1302</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Henry II of Rodez</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry II was Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rodez">Rodez</a> in the late 13th century, ruling the comital part of the city and lands in the Rouergue. He was a patron of troubadour poetry and himself took part in poetic debates, and the poet Guiraut Riquier spent his last years at his court. Through his daughter Cécile the county passed to the house of Armagnac.</p></div>
